    "text": "Consider a hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Let the&nbsp;tangent at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math> meet the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and latus rectum at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> is a&nbsp;focus of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math> which is nearer to the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, then the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;(in sq. units) is equal to",
